---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProofChain from '../components/ProofChain.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/stffnpndt/tbs-trade-proof';

const locks = [
  {
    title: 'Straight from the exchange',
    text: 'A separate program reads every fill from OKX with a read-only key and copies OKX’s own values: order ID, size, price, fee and time. It cannot place orders and is not part of the trading system.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Chained',
    text: 'Each line contains a fingerprint (hash) of the line before it. Change or delete one line, for example to hide a losing trade, and every fingerprint after it breaks.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Timestamped on Bitcoin',
    text: 'After every update, GitHub, not our computer, stamps the newest link of the chain with OpenTimestamps. The stamp ends up in the Bitcoin blockchain and proves the record existed at that time.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Archived',
    text: 'Every version of the record is also saved to the Wayback Machine of the Internet Archive, an independent copy we do not control.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Trade proof | Trading B(u)y Signal"
  description="Every trade is published within a minute in a public record that cannot be changed afterwards, and anyone can check it."
>
  <section class="head dark grain">
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">Trading B(u)y Signal</a>
      <a class="back" href="/">Back to start page</a>
    </header>
    <div class="wrap intro">
      <h1>Trade proof</h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        Every trade is published within a minute, in a public record that cannot be changed
        afterwards, not even by us. Anyone can check it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap visual">
      <ProofChain />
      <p class="links-row">
        <a class="more on-dark" href={`${REPO}/blob/main/journal.jsonl`}>Open the record</a>
        <a class="more on-dark" href={REPO}>The repository on GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block grain" aria-labelledby="rec-title">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">1. The record</p>
      <h2 id="rec-title">What is recorded</h2>
      <p>
        Every order the system places on OKX Europe is filled by the exchange, and every fill is
        written to a public record, the journal, about a minute later. Nothing is selected and
        nothing is left out.
      </p>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li><strong>Every fill</strong> on the futures account, with the exchange’s own order ID, size, price, fee and time.</li>
        <li><strong>Every closed position</strong> as reported by the exchange, with its realized result, including liquidations.</li>
        <li><strong>Which strategy</strong> placed the order, taken from the trading system’s own records.</li>
        <li><strong>Orders placed by hand</strong>, if there ever are any, marked as such.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top: 1.75rem !important">
        The record starts with the trades from 13 October 2026, when live trading began in its
        current form. Those first trades were added on 17 October from the exchange’s history and
        are marked as such; everything since then is recorded live.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block dark grain" aria-labelledby="lock-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">2. Why it cannot be changed</p>
      <h2 id="lock-title">Four locks</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        A track record is only worth something if nobody can quietly improve it later. These four
        locks make sure that every change would show.
      </p>
      <ol class="locks" data-locks>
        {locks.map((l, i) => (
          <li style={`--i:${i}`}>
            <span class="lamp" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h3>{l.title}</h3>
            <p>{l.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block grain" aria-labelledby="check-title">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">3. Check it yourself</p>
      <h2 id="check-title">You do not have to trust us</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Read the record</h3>
          <p>
            The journal is a plain text file with one entry per line. Its full history of changes
            is on <a href={`${REPO}/commits/main`}>GitHub</a>.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Check the chain</h3>
          <p>
            Download the repository and run <code>python verify.py</code>. It recalculates every
            fingerprint and reports any line that was changed, removed or reordered.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Check a timestamp</h3>
          <p>
            The timestamps are on the <a href={`${REPO}/tree/proofs/heads`}>proofs branch</a>.
            Drop one <code>.txt</code> file and its <code>.ots</code> file on <a href="https://opentimestamps.org">opentimestamps.org</a>{" "}
            to see when it entered the Bitcoin blockchain.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Compare with the exchange</h3>
          <p>
            With read-only access to the account, <code>python verify.py --okx</code> matches every
            line with OKX’s own records and reports any fill that is missing from the journal.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block dark grain" aria-labelledby="limit-title">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kicker">4. Read it right</p>
      <h2 id="limit-title">What it shows, and what it does not</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>It covers the trading account the system runs on. It cannot show that no other accounts exist.</li>
        <li>The journal holds the raw fills in contract sizes, as they happened. The forward test on the start page turns the closed trades into a comparable result with a fixed $10,000 per strategy.</li>
        <li>Funding payments on futures are booked separately by the exchange and are not part of the fills.</li>
        <li>One order often fills in several pieces at slightly different prices, so a single trade can appear as several lines.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top: 1.75rem !important">
        The record shows what was traded. It is not a promise about future results, and nothing on
        this site is financial advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Head ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  .head {
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }
  .site-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 1.75rem clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .wordmark {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .back {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--on-dark-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .back:hover {
    color: var(--gold-bright);
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.75rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #f2f1ee;
  }
  .tagline {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem);
    color: var(--on-dark-muted);
  }
  .visual {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .links-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 2rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .more {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #f2f1ee;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--gold);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1.5px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .more:hover {
    color: var(--gold-bright);
  }

  /* Blocks ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .block {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem);
  }
  .narrow > * {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem !important;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gold) !important;
  }
  .block:not(.dark) .kicker {
    color: #8a6d33 !important;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .dark h2 {
    color: #f2f1ee;
  }
  .block p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .dark p {
    color: var(--on-dark-muted);
  }
  .block a {
    text-decoration-color: var(--gold);
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .dark h3 {
    color: #f2f1ee;
  }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SFMono-Regular', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.875em;
    background: rgba(26, 27, 29, 0.07);
    padding: 0.08em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .plain {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .dark .plain {
    color: var(--on-dark-muted);
  }
  .plain li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .note {
    max-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gold);
    margin: 0 !important;
  }
  .lead {
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  /* Locks ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .locks {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .locks li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.5rem 3.25rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .locks p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .lamp {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.5rem;
    top: 1.85rem;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid var(--on-dark-muted);
    transition:
      background-color 300ms ease calc(var(--i) * 220ms),
      border-color 300ms ease calc(var(--i) * 220ms),
      box-shadow 300ms ease calc(var(--i) * 220ms);
  }
  [data-locks].lit .lamp {
    background: var(--gold-bright);
    border-color: var(--gold-bright);
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px 2px rgba(230, 201, 136, 0.55);
  }

  /* Steps ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }
  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    position: relative;
    padding: 1rem 0 0 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .steps li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.85rem;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: #8a6d33;
  }
  .steps p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .locks {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .locks {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const list = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-locks]');
  if (list) {
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(
      ([e]) => {
        if (e.isIntersecting) {
          list.classList.add('lit');
          io.disconnect();
        }
      },
      { threshold: 0.4 },
    );
    io.observe(list);
  }
</script>
